
# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Environment variables and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Testing and coverage
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Linters and type checkers
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# IDE and editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log

# Generated media
storage/audio/*
storage/images/*
storage/videos/*

# Preserve directory placeholders
!storage/audio/.gitkeep
!storage/images/.gitkeep
!storage/videos/.gitkeep

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/
```

### One important decision

We're ignoring generated media, not the entire `storage/` directory. Later, we'll use `.gitkeep` files to ensure Git preserves the empty directory structure.

**Your task:** Create and save `.gitignore`.

Then we'll create `.env.example` and configure how ContentFactory handles provider credentials without exposing secrets.